2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01UkvHVso8GQy2ZJUH9csaCf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18 across us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.1 has an unhealthy record in production. Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.3.1-rc was only in staging and was also unhealthy). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator partial-failure error, leaving the service mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed in all three regions. Post-rollback status: healthy=true, error rate 0.002, all regions on v2.3.0. Follow-ups: investigate the v2.3.1 failure, and the orchestrator partial failure during rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-2024"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, and it may or may not have gone through. I'll check the incident list before retrying so I don't page on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01FtSPBTmfyk2WBFXZ6HAVFh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18). The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy. v2.3.1 is unhealthy, and v2.3.1-rc only ran in staging. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed across regions. I retried the same rollback, and it completed everywhere. No change-manager approval was needed because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** The first attempt to open the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying, and INC-0001 already existed with the full summary, so I did not create a duplicate. It records the rollback, the partial failure, and the retry. Its follow-ups are to investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure during rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}